.TH SORTOF-PALSCORE 1 "October 2026" "sortof-suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sortof\-palscore \- list JPEG video frames in scene order
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sortof\-palscore
[options] LIST|\-|DIR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds scenes in a list of JPEG pictures and writes the list in scene order. Each JPEG is decoded at one eighth scale and reduced to a small signature: coarse histograms of Y, Cb and Cr plus a grid of mean luma. Noise barely changes a signature, so scenes show up although their JPEG rows never match byte for byte.
.PP
A file starts a new scene when its distance from the last few files of the current scene is above the cut (\-c). In the output scenes stay whole and in natural order inside; after each scene the most similar unvisited scene follows if it is within \-j percent, otherwise, or if the natural next scene is within \-b percent of that best one, the natural next scene follows. Byte\-identical files are chained right behind their first instance (\-D, on by default).
.PP
Given folders, it makes the natural list itself, as sortof\-natural would. The signatures are kept in a file and reused while the list is the same, so tuning takes seconds. A set's specs.txt is added to the end of the list by itself. Files that are not JPEGs get no signature and are placed at the end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o FILE
Write the list in scene order.
.TP
.B \-v FILE
Write one line per scene to FILE.
.TP
.B \-w FILE
Signature file (made if missing or if the list changed). Default: LIST.bin, or DIR.bin beside a folder.
.TP
.B \-F
Force the signatures to be made again.
.TP
.B \-c PCT
Scene cut: the distance above which a file starts a scene (default 10).
.TP
.B \-k K
Files looked back at for the cut (default 4).
.TP
.B \-j PCT
Follow the most similar unvisited scene only if it is within PCT (default 5).
.TP
.B \-b PCT
Prefer the natural next scene if it is within PCT of the best one (default 1).
.TP
.B \-g N
Most scenes used for the look\-alike search and the order (default 60000).
.TP
.B \-D
Chain byte\-identical files behind their first instance (the default, with \-o).
.TP
.B \-N
No duplicate chaining.
.TP
.B \-t N
Threads.
.TP
.B \-p PATH
Pin PATH: it comes first in the \-o list and is never read. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
sortof\-palscore SET/ep1 \-o list.txt
zfrag pack \-T list.txt \-o ep1.tar.zfrag
.RE
.fi
.sp
